      "intel_summary": "All 5 evaluated source IPs (203.0.113.30, 203.0.113.13, 203.0.113.15, 203.0.113.18, and 203.0.113.35) were flagged as 'malicious'. They all fall within the CIDR block 203.0.113.0/24 and are categorized as botnet infrastructure actively associated with distributed credential-stuffing campaigns.",
      "enrichment_notes": "Threat intelligence strongly corroborates the detection of a distributed credential-stuffing attack. The fact that 100% of the sampled IPs (5 of 5) are known malicious botnet nodes associated with credential-stuffing campaigns substantially increases the certainty that this traffic is malicious and coordinated rather than accidental failed logins or scanner noise. However, the immediate severity is tempered by the fact that all 15 attempts failed (HTTP 401) with zero successful logins, indicating that no accounts were compromised during this specific window. Protective measures (such as rate limiting or IP-range blocking on 203.0.113.0/24) are warranted to prevent further attempts.",
